]. Laboratory culture using nutrient-rich media can readily capture less than 1% of soil microorganisms, and the recovery percentage varies across environments, with higher counts in eutrophic settings like gut microbiomes. Innovative culture methods utilizing lower nutrient levels and extracts from natural environments prove effective in obtaining cultures from underrepresented bacterial phyla, especially when employing solid media [
