], and these methods, although yielding novel phylogenetic and chemical diversity, are time-consuming and necessitate focused attention on specific strains for optimal natural product discovery. Despite these limitations, these approaches persist in delivering unique contributions to both phylogenetic and chemical diversity, acting in tandem with culture-independent methods.
